(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#" :text "Falsifiable coverage for system/context! discovering ASL_CLI_ROOT when bin/asl's env is absent: spawns the stage-0 host directly (capture!/captureWith! run childEnv!, which always drops ASL_CLI_* from the child) running a probe module that calls context!, from a cwd inside the repo, a cwd outside the repo with no env (procExePath, the running exe, climbs to the root), a cwd outside the repo with only ASL_CLI_ARGV0 pointing at the exe, and a cwd outside the repo with only PATH naming it. Every case past the exe one runs a copy of the host placed outside the repo (prelude from ASL_PRELUDE), so its own exe climbs to no root and the ASL_CLI_ARGV0, PATH and failure branches are what decides. The expected root comes from git rev-parse, independent of the discovery code under test.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#makeOutsideCwd!" :text "a cwd no workspace root is above: proves the cwd walk alone cannot resolve it, forcing the exe fallback")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#makePathDir!" :text "a PATH entry named asl-host, pointing at the real host, for the onPath! candidate")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#makeOutsideExeCopy!" :text "a file outside any repo: realPath resolves it, but climbing from its dir finds no .git/rules.asn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#makeDeniedCandidate!" :text "sub has no permission bits: stat of anything inside it fails EACCES, not ENOENT")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#removeDeniedCandidate!" :text "restore execute bits before removing: the owner can always chmod back, even a 000 dir")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#runProbeEnv!" :text "captureWith! runs childEnv!, which always drops ASL_CLI_* names; extra puts back only what a case needs")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#expectedRoot!" :text "ground truth independent of discoverRoot!, so the test cannot pass by agreeing with itself")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#resolveHostBin" :text "asl test strips ASL_CLI_HOST_BIN like any other ASL_CLI_* name; ASL_HOST survives, so prefer it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#checkSelfExeCase!" :text "no ASL_CLI_* and no asl-host on PATH: only the running exe's own path can name the root")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#makeOutsideHost!" :text "a runnable host copy outside the repo: its own exe climbs to no root, so the later cases test their own branch")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#checkArgv0OutsidePathInRepoCase!" :text "ARGV0 resolves but climbs to no root: r1 stops there; r2 must still find root via PATH")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#checkPermissionDeniedCase!" :text "a hard stat fault on the only candidate must surface, not collapse into the generic give-up")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/rootDiscoveryTest.asl#checkGiveUpMessageCase!" :text "the give-up message must name what it tried, not just repeat ASL_CLI_ROOT is unset")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#" :text "Native asl-cli with no bin/asl wrapper (plan RT unit T2): bin/asl build compiles asl-cli/src/command.asl into a binary under the workspace's .asl/tmp, then env -i with PATH only runs it from a cwd outside the workspace, by absolute path and by a PATH symlink named asl, on check of a good file, an unbalanced file and a file with an unknown symbol. With no ASL_CLI_* in the environment and no workspace above the cwd, only the binary's own path can name the root, so a pass means the binary discovered it and ran the stage-0 host it found there.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#Outcome.label" :text "case name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#Outcome.got" :text "the run")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#Outcome.exitCode" :text "wanted exit status")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#Outcome.receipt" :text "wanted last stdout line")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#Outcome.stderrHas" :text "wanted stderr substring")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#build!" :text "the binary sits inside the workspace, so its own path climbs to the root")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#setupOutside!" :text "a cwd with the three fixtures and a PATH dir whose asl links to the binary, none under the workspace")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#runClean!" :text "env -i: the child sees PATH and nothing else, as from a clean login with no wrapper")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/standaloneCliTest.asl#runTests" :text "outcomes first; both temp dirs go before the cleanup asserts")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/testChangedTest.asl#" :text "changed-suite CLI selection, execution and error integration")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/watchTest.asl#" :text "Tests for salsa-based incremental watch engine")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#" :text "the asl command: argv dispatch of every bin/asl arm (help, version, eval, forms, tools, target, pack, note, test, run, check, audit); bin/asl resolves the workspace and execs this module on asl-host")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#Open.closer" :text "the delimiter that closes it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#Open.pos" :text "character index of the opener")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#Open.opener" :text "the opening delimiter")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#main" :text "The asl command on argv; ok carries the exit code.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#retired!" :text "asl-core knows only kebab builtins; its commands retire")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#intel!" :text "asl-host child running asl-intel main; the native CLI runs intel in process (native.asl intel!)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#forms!" :text "asl-forms mainText! in process, printed with trailing newlines stripped as command.asl forms! prints its asl-host child")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#intel!" :text "asl-intel runIntel! over the CLI root in process, printed as asl-intel main prints")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#intelAlias" :text "the intel subcommand a top-level verb aliases, as command.asl dispatch! maps it; empty for any other verb")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#scan" :text "the check bin/asl ran in python, by code point")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#keywordHead?" :text "re.match \\(:[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*[\\s)]")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#asnEcho" :text "a keyword-headed form is ASN data, printed back\nA keyword-headed form printed back with exit 0, or an ERR_ASN_SYNTAX receipt with exit 2.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#crawler!" :text "CR1 ported bin/asl-crawler to the crawler package, so the crawler arm runs its ASL entry on the host")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#outputLine" :text "one output line, as println adds the newline")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#cliResult!" :text "WR1 ported bin/lens and bin/consilium into asl-cli lensCmd and consiliumCmd; output and exit follow asl-cli cli handleDispatchResult, where a bare lens info or describe prints its usage on stdout")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#engine!" :text "EN2: engine arm runs the asl-engine package entry")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#mesh!" :text "ROOT_DIR is the workspace, as in Python")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#browserUrl" :text "the gateway port follows ASL_GATEWAY_PORT as bin/asl-gateway does, default 8765")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#browserArgs" :text "err 1 is shift 2 past the end")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#noteFields" :text "claim kind scope date, as bin/asl scanned them")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#walk!" :text "find -type f 2>/dev/null: links and unreadable dirs skipped")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#testFiles!" :text "err is the exit code after its receipt\nResolves bin/asl test's path arguments to the suite files they name, walking directories; err carries the exit code after its receipt.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#runArgv" :text "RT3: a workspace file runs through tools/nativeTest, which needs the root as cwd; an absolute file under another .asl.config.asn workspace runs from that workspace with ASL_ROOT naming the root; any other file runs on the host with its bypass reason on stderr; a workspace without tools/nativeTest runs on the host")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#dispatch!" :text "one arm per bin/asl case, in its order\nRuns the bin/asl arm named by cmd on args; the Int is the exit code.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#entry!" :text "-f FILE and - carry forms with single quotes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#" :text "process and file helpers of the asl command: the workspace context bin/asl passes, argv exec and spawn with relayed output, command lookup as bash find_cmd and command -v do")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Context.root" :text "workspace root, the parent of the directory holding bin/asl")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Context.scriptDir" :text "directory of the resolved bin/asl")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Context.argv0" :text "the program path bin/asl was invoked as")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Context.hostBin" :text "ASL_HOST, else root/asl/host/out/asl-host")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Captured.exitCode" :text "exit status")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Captured.stdout" :text "captured standard output")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Captured.stderr" :text "captured standard error")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Relay.outOpen" :text "stdout not at EOF")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Relay.errOpen" :text "stderr not at EOF")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Relay.code" :text "exit status once reaped")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Relay.out" :text "captured stdout, empty when relayed")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#Relay.errText" :text "captured stderr, empty when relayed")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#pathPresence!" :text "notFound means absent, keep climbing; any other errno (permissionDenied, ...) is a real fault to report, not paper over")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#rootMarkers!" :text "a workspace root holds both .git (file in a worktree, dir in a clone) and the rules source")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#walkToRoot!" :text "climb parents until the markers show up, a hard stat error surfaces, or the filesystem root is reached")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#exeCandidates!" :text "candidates for the running exe's own path, tried in turn: the exe itself (procExePath, how a native asl-cli finds its root with no wrapper and no environment), bin/asl's recorded $0 in ASL_CLI_ARGV0, then an asl-host on PATH")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#tryCandidates!" :text "try every candidate, not just the first that resolves: one exe path can resolve and still climb to no root (a symlink farm, a container), so the rest must still get a turn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#discoverRoot!" :text "cwd first (the common case); a hard cwd error is fatal, missing markers fall through to the exe")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#giveUpMessage!" :text "say what was tried: a bare ASL_CLI_ROOT-is-unset message gives no lead on why discovery failed too")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#context!" :text "bin/asl exports the paths bash resolved; without it, discover the root from cwd or the exe")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#childEnv!" :text "children see the environment bash would pass")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#run!" :text "a child whose output passes through, as bash runs it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#runMerged!" :text "2>&1: child stderr joins our stdout")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#captureWith!" :text "capture! with extra child env, for probes that need a name childEnv! would otherwise strip or inherit")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#executable?" :text "test -x: any execute bit, dirs included")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#onPath!" :text "command -v for a name without a slash")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#trimLeft" :text "bash [:space:] trim at the start")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/system.asl#stripTrailingNewlines" :text "command substitution drops trailing newlines")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl#route!" :text "The verb and arguments entry! dispatches for args: a leading form or keyword with leading space trimmed, test for an existing .asl file (or any file under asl-eval), else the first argument as the verb; the native binary routes with it too.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#main" :text "Entry of the natively built asl binary: the workspace context, then entry!, which runs host-free verbs in process and hands every other verb to command.asl's dispatch!; no workspace exits 2 with ERR_NO_WORKSPACE.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#Done" :text "A finished sweep run: its index in the plan, suite path, exit code, last output line and full output.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#workspace!" :text "The sweep root: ASL_ROOT resolved when set, else git's top level, else the current directory.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#timeoutWanted!" :text "Per-suite timeout in seconds from ASL_SWEEP_TIMEOUT_S, 300 by default, an error when it is not an integer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#jobsWanted!" :text "Parallel job count from ASL_JOBS, the CPU count when unset, an error when it is not an integer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#changedReport!" :text "Prints each selected run in plan order as (:pass ...) or (:fail ...) with its exit and last line, then the (:changed ...) summary; exits 1 when any run failed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#changedDry!" :text "Prints the suites a changed run would select and a (:changed ...) summary with nothing run; exits 0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#lastLine" :text "The last line of text after trimming, CRLF read as LF.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#appendFileHashIn" :text "each line names path as given and hashes the file it denotes under root, so a root-relative deps closure keys the same in every worktree of identical content")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#seedTriple" :text "arm64-apple-darwin25.1.0 -> arm64-apple-darwin, the key asl/seed/seed.asn rows use (tools/seed.asl tripleKey)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#checkedInSeed!" :text "the bootstrap compiler comes from the checked-in seed: the manifest row for this triple names a .gz whose size and sha256 must match before it is unpacked, and whose IR must match llBytes/llSha256 before clang links it; the binary is kept under the cache keyed by llSha256")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#ensureSeed!" :text "ASL_NATIVE_ASL1_SEED names a pinned binary (fixtures); otherwise the checked-in seed. A cached compiler is never promoted to seed: that is how a binary older than the sources became the bootstrap")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#fromSeed!" :text "seed -> stage1 -> stage2; a failure of the seed's own stage means the seed is older than the sources")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#buildNative!" :text "a cached compiler bootstraps first; when it fails, the seed is the one retry, and both failures are reported")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#rootRelative" :text "the seed prints absolute paths where the current asl1 prints them root-relative; both become root-relative, as asl-host prints them")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#closure!" :text "the asl1 import closure comes from a native asl1: the newest cached compiler, else the checked-in seed; asl-host runs asl1.asl deps only to bootstrap, when neither exists or the native one fails, and says so on stderr")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#rest" :text "the native asl binary: verbs that need no stage-0 host run here in process; every other verb, and a verb outside the workspace root, goes through command.asl as on asl-host")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#hostJob" :text "a suite that does not build natively is a lowering gap, not a test result: it reruns on asl-host (bin/asl's host route, command.asl) under tools/fleet/run.asl with the sweep timeout and a descendant limit, its stderr kept apart; a suite that builds and fails is never rerun")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#suite!" :text "one suite as asl-host test reports it, under the path it was given; nativeTest compiles it by its root-relative path")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#absolute" :text "nativeTest names its binaries relative to the current directory; a sweep job runs in the workspace, so it gets the absolute path")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#sweepDone!" :text "a sweep without asl-host: nativeTest compiles each suite here (cached by its root-relative path), and the binaries run under tools/fleet/run.asl, k at a time, with the sweep timeout and a descendant limit; the running executable is never started")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#hostSweep!" :text "the suites of a sweep that do not build natively rerun on asl-host, k at a time under tools/fleet/run.asl, each with a gap note; without a host each stays a failure")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#check!" :text "bare check keeps its per-file asl-host check until checker parity; the sweep around it runs here")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl#launch!" :text "launch takes the workspace root from the context, as bin/asl hands ASL_ROOT to the host run, whatever ASL_ROOT the caller has")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#plan!" :text "the suites a sweep runs: for test the discovered suites, for check the tracked .asl files whose delimiters balance, with the unbalanced ones (path, byte, evidence) beside them")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#report!" :text "prints the unbalanced files, then each failed run, then the summary; the runner names who ran the suites")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/sweep.asl#changedPlan!" :text "changed files against BASE (from git in the current directory) and the tracked suites they select")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/asl1BootstrapTest.asl#seedRepo!" :text "a fixture repository with asl/seed/seed.asn and a gzip seed for the fake triple; shaOk false records a perturbed sha256")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/asl1BootstrapTest.asl#testSeedSelection" :text "the bootstrap seed comes from the checked-in asl/seed after its sha256 checks, a failing cached compiler is retried once from the seed, and a seed that cannot build the sources is ERR_SEED_STALE")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/asl1CacheDepsTest.asl#lines" :text "ASL1CACHE-NATIVE-DEPS: the asl1 closure that keys the native compiler cache comes from a native asl1 (the newest cached one, else the seed). The context names a host that does not exist, so the closure can only come from a native asl1 (with asl-host, closure! fails); it must list the same files, in the same order, as asl-host run asl1.asl deps prints, run here once under tools/fleet/run.asl")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslColdTest.asl#envFor" :text "a cold native cache does not block the verb: with an empty ASL_NATIVE_CLI_CACHE, bin/asl test answers on asl-host with a note while a detached, bounded build holds the lock; once that build finishes, the next call is served natively (servedProbe); the build is bounded by ASL_NATIVE_CLI_TIMEOUT in its own group, and whatever is left at the end is killed by group and removed")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslColdTest.asl#cleanup!" :text "a build still holding the lock at the end is killed by its process group, then the cache is removed")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslNativeTest.asl#probe" :text "bin/asl execs the native binary for a native verb: bin/asl test on servedProbe passes only when a native asl binary, not asl-host, served it; ASL_HOST forces the host, where the same probe fails; check is not native yet and still answers through asl-host with a one-line note; a suite the native lowering rejects reruns on asl-host with a note, a suite that fails natively is never rerun; native stderr carries no NATIVE-* telemetry")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslNativeTest.asl#envWith" :text "the caller's env without ASL_HOST, which would force the host path, plus the gate's pid for the probe; ASL_NATIVE_CLI_WAIT=1 makes a cold cache wait for the native build, which takes minutes, so the limit is 1500 s")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslNativeTest.asl#binAslSplit!" :text "bin/asl with its stderr in errFile and only its stdout in Done.out")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslNativeTest.asl#freshSuite" :text "a suite no cache has seen, so the native run compiles it and nativeTest's phase lines would be printed")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/fixtures/servedBy/failingProbe.asl#runTests" :text "binAslFallbackTest: a suite that builds natively and fails its assertion; bin/asl reports the native failure and never reruns it on asl-host")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/fixtures/servedBy/servedProbe.asl#Row" :text "binAslNativeTest runs this suite through bin/asl test: it walks its own ancestors up to SERVED_STOP_PID, the gate's pid, and passes only when a native asl binary served it and no asl-host stands in that chain (on asl-host the suite runs inside asl-host itself)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/fixtures/servedBy/servedProbe.asl#chain" :text "the argv0 of each process from pid up to stop, then \"stop\"; empty when the walk never reaches stop")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/fixtures/servedBy/unsupportedProbe.asl#quote" :text "binAslFallbackTest: a top-level fn named quote is a reserved call head the native lowering rejects (ERR_NATIVE_UNSUPPORTED), while asl-host runs the suite and passes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/nativeCliTest.asl#Case" :text "each case of fixtures/argv.asn was recorded from asl-host run asl/packages/asl-cli/src/command.asl (the interpreted CLI); the natively built asl/packages/asl-cli/src/native.asl must print the same stdout and stderr and exit the same with no asl-host on disk, so a verb that still delegates to the host fails here")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/nativeCliTest.asl#tokens" :text "tokens of one case line: s:TEXT for a string, [ and ] for a vector, the atom itself otherwise")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/nativeCliTest.asl#normalize" :text "a sweep line names its runner; the golden says asl-host and the native binary says native, so the name is masked")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/nativeCliTest.asl#cliEnv" :text "a case :env row replaces the default row of the same name; a case with ASL_CLI_HOST_BIN=/nonexistent/asl-host records what the CLI says without a host, so a delegating verb is compared on its dispatch alone")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/nativeCliTest.asl#prepareSweep!" :text "the sweep workspace: a git repository inside the root's ignored cache, holding the three fixture suites under tests/ (outside a fixtures segment, so discovery sees them); nativeTest compiles a suite only inside the root, so the workspace lives there")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeCli.asl#" :text "every native CLI decision bin/asl used to make in bash: bin/asl only execs the binary its pointer file names (ASL_NATIVE_CLI_CACHE/head<root with / as _>, default ~/.asl/run/nativeCli), else command.asl on asl-host; nativeGate! runs first in the native binary, hostEntry! first in command.asl, both only in the process bin/asl exec'd (ASL_CLI_ENTRY_PID is its pid)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeCli.asl#fresh?" :text "a cached binary may run only while every file its build read (its deps list: the native.asl closure, the asl1 closure that compiled it, the prelude, libaslrt.a and asl/seed/seed.asn) is byte-equal to the snapshot copy under its src/; byte comparison needs no hash, so the native binary checks itself in milliseconds")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeCli.asl#nativeGate!" :text "in the native binary: a verb that is not native (run test parse eval launch and *.asl are) execs command.asl on asl-host at once; a native verb whose binary is stale execs asl-host with ASL_NATIVE_CLI_STALE naming it, so no stale code serves a verb and hostEntry! never execs that binary again")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeCli.asl#hostEntry!" :text "in command.asl on asl-host, unless ASL_HOST forces the host: a host verb gets the one-line note that it is not native yet (forms stay silent); a native verb execs a fresh binary when the head names one, else starts the rebuild and runs on asl-host with a note naming why; ASL_NATIVE_CLI_WAIT=1 waits for the build (ASL_NATIVE_CLI_TIMEOUT plus 60 s) and then execs the binary")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeCli.asl#startBuild!" :text "one build at a time: the lock is ASL_NATIVE_CLI_CACHE/lock/pid, created exclusively with the caller's pid and then renamed over with the builder's; a lock whose pid is dead is cleared and the claim retried once")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeCli.asl#spawnBuilder!" :text "the builder (asl/host/out/aslNativeBuild, the native build build.sh compiles with the seed asl1, else asl-host run nativeBuild.asl; ROOT CACHE --lock-owner PID) starts through sys/captureWith! (command.asl carries no tools/ import: argv parity runs it in a tree without one) as a shell that puts it in its own session (perl setsid) and exits at once with output appended to build.log and prints its pid, so the verb returns at once and the build outlives it; the builder bounds its own children")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeBuild.asl#" :text "the detached native CLI build: the committed seed (seed.asn row for clang's triple, llSha256 checked) is linked with libaslrt.a, compiles asl1 (stage 1), which compiles native.asl; each stage is cached under ASL_NATIVE_CLI_CACHE as name-key, key a sha256 over the seed row, libaslrt.a, clang's version, the compiler and every file the stage reads; the cli stage keeps its deps and a snapshot of them for nativeCli/fresh?, and the head for this root is renamed into place last")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeBuild.asl#child!" :text "every child runs through tools/fleet/run.asl with the time left of ASL_NATIVE_CLI_TIMEOUT (1800 s from the start) and ASL_NATIVE_CLI_MAXDESC (32) descendants")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeBuild.asl#compile!" :text "a compile or link that exits non-zero marks the key failed (name-key.failed), so the same sources are not rebuilt on every call; a timeout or a killed child marks nothing")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/tests/binAslStaleTest.asl#runTests" :text "a stale native binary never serves a verb: the shared cache's binary for this tree is copied into a test cache with one snapshot file edited (the binary now predates its sources) and named by that cache's head; bin/asl test then answers on asl-host with the stale note, and with ASL_NATIVE_CLI_WAIT=1 the rebuild (stages linked from the shared cache, so it only rekeys) points the head back at this tree's binary, which serves servedProbe natively")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeBuild.asl#main" :text "nativeBuild ROOT [CACHE] [--if-cold] [--lock-owner PID]: --if-cold returns at once when the head for ROOT exists (asl/host/build.sh runs it so on every build, which keeps a fresh clone hostless); the lock is released only when it names this builder or the caller that spawned it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/nativeBuild.asl#seedField" :text "nativeBuild compiles with the committed seed asl1, whose checker knows neither bytesSha256 nor sha256, so it hashes with asl/prelude/native/sha256 imported as a module and carries its own copies of asl1Cache's seed manifest helpers")
